Slop Detector — Privacy policy
Effective date: 19 September 2026
Maintainer: itsaam — https://github.com/itsaam

Purpose

Slop Detector classifies the text of posts displayed on X and Twitter according
to the definition configured by the user. It optionally blurs flagged posts.
It is not an image or video analysis service and is not affiliated with X.

Data processed in your browser

The content script reads displayed post text, quoted text, post identifiers,
and flags indicating attached media or truncated text. It also recognizes
supported platform "Made with AI" disclosures. These readings support only
the visible classification and filtering features on x.com and twitter.com.

The extension does not access direct-message bodies, cookies, passwords,
browsing history from other websites, or the contents of images and videos.
Text inside a post may itself contain names, links, or personal information.
Protected posts visible to you are not automatically excluded. Do not enable
remote analysis if you do not want such displayed content sent to a provider.

Remote analysis and consent

Remote analysis is disabled by default, including for existing settings that
do not record consent. To enable it, read the disclosure in the popup, activate
the remote-analysis switch, and save. You can turn it off and save at any time.

When enabled, post text, quoted text, media/truncation flags, your custom
definition, and model instructions are sent over HTTPS to your chosen provider:

- TypeSafe: api.typesafe.ai, for Jev inference.
- OpenRouter: openrouter.ai, which routes the Jev request to TypeSafe.

Post identifiers are used locally for caching, not included as a separate
field in inference requests. Images and videos are not uploaded. Like any
HTTPS service, the selected provider can receive connection metadata such
as your IP address. Your API key authenticates only with its matching provider.

The Test button sends a fixed example and your configured definition to the
selected provider. It does not send a post from your timeline. This user-initiated
test can be used without enabling ongoing remote analysis and may incur a charge.

Disabling analysis stops new post requests. A request already transmitted
cannot be withdrawn from the provider. Supported platform AI labels are
processed locally and do not require remote-analysis consent or an API key.

Provider handling and retention are governed by your account settings and
their policies. The extension does not promise zero provider retention or
that the provider will not use submitted data for purposes described in its
own policy. Review these before enabling analysis:
https://typesafe.ai/legal/privacy-policy
https://openrouter.ai/privacy

Local storage and deletion

API keys, your preferences, and analysis results are stored in the extension's
chrome.storage.local area. They are not synchronized through chrome.storage.sync.
This is browser-local storage, not an operating-system password vault.
Content scripts cannot read this storage; trusted extension pages and the
service worker use it to provide the configured features.

The persistent result cache holds up to 1,000 entries. Entries contain a post
identifier and configuration/content fingerprint in the cache key, plus score,
model, provider, and timestamps; raw post text is not stored in that cache.
There is no time-based expiry. Older entries are evicted when the bound is hit.
Your custom definition is stored as a preference.

Remove a saved API key by clearing its field and saving. Uninstalling the
extension removes its browser-local storage. This does not delete copies
already received by a provider; address those requests to that provider.

Limited use

Slop Detector uses the data described above only to provide its classification
and filtering features. It does not sell data, use it for advertising, collect
analytics, or send it to a maintainer-operated server. The maintainer does not
receive or read your posts or API keys. Transfers to the selected inference
provider are necessary for the remote feature that you explicitly enable.
This use is intended to comply with the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy,
including its Limited Use requirements.

Contact

Questions and deletion guidance: https://github.com/itsaam/slop-detector/issues
Issues are public. Do not include API keys, private posts, or personal data.
